# Gradual distribution drift — context distribution interpolates linearly
# between source and target over a window. Tests handling of slow
# concept drift, the common practical case (population shifts month to
# month rather than overnight).

name: synthetic_gradual
description: |
  Gradual drift. The Beta-distribution parameters interpolate linearly
  between source and target over a window of 1500 steps. There is no
  sharp change point to detect; the algorithm has to track a moving
  target. This is harder than abrupt shift in some ways (no clear signal
  for change-point detectors) and easier in others (no sudden break).
horizon: 10000
n_seeds: 20
delta: 0.05

environment:
  type: SyntheticShift
  n_arms: 10
  n_objectives: 2
  context_dim: 1
  beta: 1.0
  lipschitz_L: 4.0
  sigma: 0.1
  schedule: gradual
  shift_times: [2500, 7500]    # interpolate over [t0, t1]
  nu: 5.0

algorithms:
algorithms:
  - PCBShift
  - SukKpotufe20
  - Turgay18
  - Auer16
  - ParetoUCB
  - AnnealingPareto
  - StaticBinning
  - SlidingWindowBinning
  - CUSUMRestart
  - ATCBinning
  - Kone23
  - Cai24
  - ScalarizedUCB
  - RandomPlay

metrics:
  - PreferenceRegret
  - HausdorffRegret
  - DominanceCoverage
  - ParetoPrecisionRecall
